    },
    {
     "type": "note",
     "title": "One tense for “I live”, “I'm living” and “I'll live”",
     "md": "German has **no -ing form**. *Präsens* (present tense) covers:\n\n- now: {de:Lisa schläft.} = Lisa *is sleeping*\n- facts and habits: {de:Ich trinke Tee.} = I drink tea\n- something that started earlier and still goes on: {de:Er lernt seit zwei Jahren Deutsch.} = he *has been learning* German for two years\n- the future (with a time word): {de:Morgen habe ich frei.}\n\nTo stress “right now”, add **gerade**: {de:Ich lerne gerade Deutsch.}"
    },
    {
     "type": "table",
     "title": "Regular verbs: stem + ending",
     "intro": "Infinitive **wohn|en** → cut off *-en* → stem **wohn-** → add the ending. Tap a row to hear it.",
