     "type": "note",
     "title": "Bonus: talking about the future",
     "md": "Germans usually talk about the future with the **present tense + a time word**:\n\n- {de:Was machst du morgen?} = What are you doing tomorrow?\n- {de:Morgen kaufe ich eine Tasche.} = Tomorrow I'll buy a bag.\n- {de:Morgen habe ich frei.} = I'm off tomorrow.\n\nNotice: when *morgen* comes first, the verb is still in **2nd position** and *ich* moves after it."
